    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.59) and **Gunnar Henderson** (78.37) anchoring the lineup as the clear offensive pillars. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Anderson, where the park factors and SP skill metrics align to boost his profile significantly. Meanwhile, despite a challenging opponent in Jack Perkins, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier start, buoyed by a substantial 14% platoon efficiency gain and an assumed #3 slot in the order that maximizes his scoring ceiling. **Kyle Tucker** (75.96) and **Jackson Merrill** (69.72) also provide elite stability against Montero and Martinez, respectively, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefiting from a 13% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage.\n\nStrategic priority has been placed on the stolen base category, driving the selection of **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.27), both of whom are projected to capitalize on the weak SP_xERA of Ober. **Drake Baldwin** is an intriguing play at 68.73, largely due to his spot in the leadoff position, which offers a 10% efficiency bump. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Dominic Smith**, who finished with a respectable 52.48 score but was relegated to the bench because he lacked the positional versatility and relative efficiency of our starting infielders. **Coby Mayo** also fell just shy of the threshold; despite his power upside, his 49.05 score was suppressed by a poor platoon match against Perkins, leading us to favor the more consistent plate appearance projections of **Tommy White** and **Nasim Nunez**. \n\nManagers should remain attentive to the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Tommy White**, and **Luis Lara**, as any mid-day shifts in batting order could necessitate immediate lineup optimization to protect our category standings. While **Heliot Ramos** (59.87) carries a slight risk facing a lefty, his inclusion is tactical; we are banking on his sprint speed and a favorable 2% situational bump against a slow-delivery pitcher to bolster our stolen base count. All starters should be monitored for weather developments, though current projections suggest no extreme conditions will impact game flow.",
